Heatmap of Upregulated Genes:
The most highly upregulated genes in SC/B showed relatively low expression in BM, SP, and LN.

Biological Interpretation
These genes are highly expressed in SC/B and have lower expression in BM, LN, and SP. They include genes involved in cell signaling, stress responses, and cell survival, indicating that leukemic cells in SC/B have a different gene expression pattern from the other tissues.

Heatmap of Downregulated Genes:
Genes that were downregulated in SC/B remained highly expressed in peripheral tissues.

Biological Interpretation
These genes have lower expression in SC/B and higher expression in BM, LN, and SP. Many of them are involved in protein synthesis and oxidative phosphorylation. This shows that these processes have lower activity in SC/B compared with the other tissues.
